Hokay folks, this is a long one, but given that this is my first real
(non-exploring mode, no deaths, competitive) ascension and I've been
playing this stinking game since 1990, I feel entitled to vent. Enjoy
or endure, as you please.


Somewhere in the highest heavens, there is a loud, roaring bar where
the demigods and demigoddesses of nethack congregate.  There's a party
at the Rowdy Rubber Chicken every night,  and it's a party that makes
towns like Rio or New Orleans weep from inadequacy.  But that's
nothing compared to the party on that special night, the night a new
visitor pushes her way past the Archon bouncers to order the
traditional round for the house.   Tonight is such a night.

Our visitor is short and ugly, clinking in silver dragon scale mail, a
+4 halberd slung over the shoulder, Magicbane tucked in the belt, and
a cockatrice corpse held loosely in one gloved hand.  The sex is
indistinguishable under the armor and cloak except for the piping high
voice marking her as a bearer of the double-x chromosome.  When one of
the dumber barbarian demigods makes a move, her eyes flash, her hands
glow red and deal him a quick punch, causing him to stagger and
stumble off in the arms of his friends.   Glorfindel', an elf, is
intrigued and moves in to talk to the newcomer.

"Magic user, huh?" 
"Not really.  My religion forbids magic.  But I do supernatural stuff
like fireballs through the power of my God working through me".

"Whatever.  But why don't you just use the normal terms just for now? 
Ya know, magic, wizard?  You can call it grape jelly if you like, but
I won't understand what you're saying.  So why don't you tell me your
story?  You've given us three paragraphs of introduction and it's
about time to get to the adventure."

"All right&#8230;." 

Shoshana was the latest in a long, long, line of wizards.  Most of the
early ones had been human, had survived for five levels, then been
promptly ambushed in the tunnels by a floating eye or a soldier ant. 
One had got so far as the Medusa level before falling into a pit while
wielding a cockatrice corpse.  That's when the Deity decided to switch
to gnome avatars, as the infravision provided some early warning
against these disasters.  The early gnomes died horribly and died
young, one after only ten turns  after kicking a locked chest one too
many times.    So I went back to human avatars.  These died horribly
too.  Then back to gnomes. Most of them died horribly, but three or
four of them showed real promise.  Then came Shoshana.

Shoshana didn't look like much compared to the past three dead
candidates.  She had crap starting equipment. No means of engraving
elbereth.  Useless potions.  Useless rings.  Useless scrolls.  And a
new moon on top of it.    Nonetheless, she was unusual for a gnome,
starting with a strength of 15 and an intelligence of 19.  Thus, when
by a fluke she found a crystal plate mail in the first five floors of
the dungeon she was able to take advantage of it.   That solved most
of the armor class problems. Then she found a wand of digging, which
saved her life from the killer bees by enabling her to engrave
Elbereth. This plus her infravision gave her the ability to not be
surprised (often),  to avoid unfavorable combat, and to gain a
relative measure of safety when pressed too hard.

Traveled down to gnome minetown, which was far simpler than it would
otherwise be.  Nonetheless, Shoshana's vicious pet cat "persuaded" (to
her distress) one of the dwarfs to yield his pickaxe, which she then
took back up and into sokoban.  Sokoban was completed while breaking
only one boulder, and from this she got an uncursed bag of holding and
a halberd.  She used the halberd to engage enemies at long range,
further compensating for her weak armor class.

Back down into the mines.  Here her infravision saved her life by
allowing her to see and avoid the lethal gargoyles and
polytrap-generated mumak which had ambushed and killed so many of her
human predecessors.    The non-cellar ending at the bottom of the
mines revealed a loadstone (which she discovered by trying to kick it
and nearly breaking her foot in the process), a touchstone, and an
uncursed luckstone which never got blessed through the duration of the
game.

Nonetheless, her bad luck continued.  She ate dozens of corpses and
gained no intrinsics whatever.  Blue jellies ,red molds, spiders,
killer bees - many hurt, but no intrinsics came.  Also, there was not
ONE SHOP in the entirety of the maze from top to bottom. NOT ONE,
outside of minetown, and those were largely full of crud.

I was tempted to throw the character away. But she (and I) persevered,
and gradually things turned around.
A floating eye donated telepathy. A wand of create monster allowed her
to go on a sacrificing spree at a friendly (neutral) alter at level 3.
 This resulted in magicbane - THAT was promising.  Then a tengu came
along and happily donated the teleport control intrinsic.  With that,
it was no trouble at all to hunt up some nymph street trash to gain
teleportitis.  With crystal plate armor, a wand for engraving, an
artifact weapon and the ability to teleport at will anywhere, the
character began to pick up speed.   I was convinced I would die by
being disintegrated by black dragon breath, so I spent considerable
time blindfolded to get early warning of this.

It was about this point that the close calls began to happen. An
elf-lord knocked her down to 3 or so hitpoints with a wand of cold,
but a quick prayer saved her life.  The wand took her down again but
she saved herself with the extra healing spell before finally taking
this tough dude down.  But it was worth it, as he donated the sleep
resistant intrinsic.  On down.

Found a bigroom on level 10 and a bones file on level 11 for a
character who had died after the castle.  She left behind a 0:0 wand
of wishing, which will be mentioned again later.

Fort Ludios was discovered on level 12 thanks to "detect treasure".  I
stupidly hit this level , and nearly died at the hands of a pair of
elf-lords, who got me down to 1 hit point before prayer again saved my
life.   Went back through the portal to rest and re-charge, then back
through  to fight some more, then back to recharge, then back through.
  I cleared the first room, but the dragons did not look friendly so I
retreated and resumed  my descent through the dungeon.

Continued down and found more alters (which I converted) and a portal
to the quest on level 14.  Momentarily I was level 14 as well and took
the portal to see my old teacher Neferet the Green. The story of his
struggle with the Dark One is well known, so let us skip to the part
where I am descending down towards the Dark One's tower.  At the
bottom level I started not paying attention and a band of critters
again brought me down to 1 hit point, but this time a potion of full
healing saved my life.

Down to see the Dark One.  There wasn't much subtlety - I snuck into
the room in elven boots, dispatched his guards, hit him one time with
Magicbane and then made a controlled teleport to the stairs.  I only
had to wait about two turns before the Dark One materialized amidst
threats and promises.  yeah, yeah.  With my cloak of magic resistance
I was immune to most of his damage and with me blocking the stairs he
couldn't escape.  He was immune to most power so I simply beat him to
death with Magicbane, taking the Bell of Opening. Then I let the
prisoners out of their cells and let them stagger to their freedom,
blinking in the harsh light of a sun many of them had not seen in
years.   Found many books, including a cursed book and a magic marker.
 I took panes to uncurse the book and was rewarded for my pains with a
book of fireball!

Back to the main branch.  More alters, more sacrifices result in
Giantslayer (yecch - "Use my gift wisely" - with all due respect, the
wisest thing I can do is to put it in a chest and leave it there), a
crowning, and a blessed spellbook of Finger of Death! YES!

Tried to decide between hitting Fort Ludios again and hitting the
castle.  Went back up to Ludios. I quickly realized my mistake when a
blast of fire from a red dragon cooked my armor.  I was fire-resistant
- no trouble there - but I was perilously close to losing my cloak of
magic resistance.    Still I killed them with magic missile and
fireball (amazing what that does to tightly packed soldiers) then hit
Croesus' vault itself.  A black dragon - my great fear - made an
appearance.   I blasted away with fireball, since the dragon was just
out of sight north of the door but I used telepathy to see him and
target the square next to him.  I ran out of juice.  He trundled out
over the moat, and there occurred a slow and bizarre dance in which
Shoshana desparately twisted to make sure the dragon never had a
direct shot, while waiting for her energy to re-charge enough to blast
the thing dead and at the same time lure it over land where she could
eat it and gain the coveted disintegration resistance.  But her
efforts were for naught as a forest centaur inside the castle shot at
her with a crossbow bolt, which missed and hit the dragon instead. 
With a despairing cry it fell splash into the moat and disappeared,
matched only by Shoshana's equally desparing cry "NOOOOOO!"

Well, so much for that.   Went into the vault with a pair of water
walking boots from the bones level, finished off the bad guys, then
went through the entire vault carefully disarming each and every land
mine. Not one was set off, at least not by me.  Found a magic marker
somewhere in here as well.

Back out of the vault for my first and only encounter with a mind
flayer.  Just kept blasting away until it got close enough to attack,
but all attacks were blessedly blocked by my helmet before the
creature went down.

Found a scroll of genocide, which I used to wipe out master mind
flayers.



Then I had an idea - I took the marker and a second one I found to the
cache of scrolls I'd been keeping.  I wrote a second scroll of
genocide (bye-bye mind flayers), then wrote a second, blessed it and
used it wipe out all L. (HalleLUjah!)

It was at this time I began thinking the character might go all the
way, and began praying really hard (OUT of game in the real world)
that God would protect this character and let me see it through. It
HAS been thirteen years after all.

Perhaps he listened , but things did begin to get a bit easier.  Of
course, it helped that I had been sacrificing to become extremely
lucky and fed gems identified with touchstone to gray unicorns.

Continued searching found a book of create monster.   Worthless
clerical spell.  Blanked it in water, then used the marker to re-write
it as a book of identify. THAT really helped the game.   More alters
followed by sacrifices resulted in crowning (and intrinsics) and a
book of Finger of Death. YEE-HAH!  Of course, now I expected Medusa to
kill me.
  
Down to the Medusa level where there was no Titan encounter I had been
dreading.  A couple of fireballs in the water coupled with warning saw
off the eels without trouble.  A troll or two wandered up, which I
first dispatched, then threw their corpses in the water.  A few
minutes later I saw the message "The troll rises from the dead!  The
troll drowns"  Heh heh heh.

Then a couple of water trolls came after me as well.  I had no idea
whether the two were connected, but I wasn't in the mood so I just
ran.  A quick hike across the water in water walking boots brought me
to Medusa's house, which I entered blindfolded armed with a looking
glass, which killed her instantly.

Further down I met my first nurses, which I danced with to build HP. 
This got me in a jam - I dropped my bag of holding to become
unburdened and was dancing with a nurse when a sasquatch moved in to
join the party.  I teleported away from him to the nurse and suddenly
saw I was weak, in desparate need of food.  I couldn't teleport again.
 There's a sasquatch standing between me and my bag of holding (and
it's food).  And there's a nurse pounding on me.  And I'm naked
without a weapon.

Didn't know what else to do, so attacked the sasquatch bare-handed,
killed it, and ate it.  This horrified the nurse, who ran away.  I
chased her down and gave her a little love tap to get her attention. 
Unfortunately I tapped a little too hard and had to resume the mission
without finishing the dance.    That was only the most impressive one
- I'd learned the hard way about using power when naked from a
previous character, who when attacked by a creature while nurse
dancing had hit it with a FOD, had the FOD bounce back, and kill him
instantly.  So occasionally some small critter like a gecko would
happen along and I would pummel it with fists, feet, and teeth.  This
happened often enough that I was able to advance to basic skill in
hand-to-hand combat.

Proceeding on down, I found Fire Brand just lying around, which I
immediately put to use.

Down to the castle level. I cleared the surrounding eels and xorns
with fireball, then blew down the drawbridge with force bolt. I then
stood at a distance and fired magic missile, finger of death, and
fireball through the door at the tightly packed soldiers within. 
trapped on the far side of the moat, they could do nothing but walk up
to the edge of the moat and stand there looking stupid as hellish fire
came down on them.  Just as my energy ran dry, a giant had the bright
idea of zapping me with a wand of cold.  It didn&#8217;t hurt me at
all, but the cold beam froze the moat.  This allowed the creatures to
storm across the moat and come after me.  Outnumbered and out of
charge, I ran for the stairs and made it up to recharge.
Healed up and recovered my energy points, then went back down, cut my
way through the few monsters on this side of the moat, then used
fireball to melt the moat and restore the previous tactical situation.
 Killed most of the monsters by remote, then used water walking to
cross into the castle and finish the job.

 FINALLY got a ring of levitation and an amulet of life saving!   The
Castle throne gave me a wish, the first time I have EVER gotten a wish
from a throne.  I promptly wished for +2 silver dragon scale mail and
ditched the useful - but heavy - crystal plate mail.

There was a black dragon amongst the dragons in the hall way.  Two
FODS finished 3 and gave me the distintegration resistance I'd been
worried about.    The fourth was a silver dragon, which I beat to
death with Magicbane.  The castle armor had a cornuthaum and a pair of
boots of speed, which I promptly put to good use.  However, I carried
down a pair of elvish boots of well so I could act stealthily at need.
The castle wand of wishing had only one charge in it, which I burned
on a scroll of charging.  I then re-charged and wished for a magic
marker.  I used the marker to lower my AC, then realized there was
only one priest in the entire dungeon in a temple - in minetown.  I
went there and dumped all the gold in croesus' vault in exchange for 9
points of protection, then prepared to descend into the valley of the
dead, armed among other things with a ring of conflict and a  wand of
wishing with two charges, figuring they might be able to get me out of
a scrape.  And down I went. ..
At first my stealth allowed me to fight the creatures one at a time,
but I stepped on a squeaky board, they all woke up and I had my hands
full I put on my ring, forcing the creatures to spend more time
fighting each other than fighting me.  I kept the Vampires and Vampire
Lords at a distance with my halberd (now +2), advancing to skilled
with the weapon so that I could hit any point within two squares of my
character with it.  Eventually cut my way through the group and 
looted a lot of books from the chests.  I tamed a Vampire Lord  with a
scroll of taming.   I also had a magic harp from much earlier which I
was holding on to for just such an emergency, but I used the scroll
instead.  The  Vampire Lord (named Spike) helped defend me and
eventually killed Moloch's priest on this level - I hadn't wanted to
leave this minion alive, but had no desire to lose my telepathy, so I
walked up to the guy and blew my magic whistle to bring Spike in and
do my dirty work for me. Alas, the books he had were either useless or
ones I already had copies of.    I put them all in a chest by the
stairs and engraved Elbereth under it to protect it.  Went on and
stopped at the door to Gehennon.

And turned back. Well, executed a tactical withdrawal, anyway.  My
spell time-outs were all hitting bottom, so I went back up to collect
all the different books and important stuff from the various caches
from the top of the mazes to the bottom and put the important stuff 
in my castle cache where the throne used to be.   Gathered all the
food I would need,  sacrificed and got the gift of stealth which
allowed me to leave behind the elven boots, went to Mine Town and
bought 7 candles from Izhak, gathered some holy water, re-memorized
all the important stuff - and left Firebrand behind in the chest.  It
had been made rusty,  I already had a +4 rustproof Magicbane
(over-enchanted by accident), and I didn't see what use it would be in
Gehennom.  So Firebrand stayed and I  went back down.

I also made a list of the likely things that would kill me from this
point on:

*Die of Illness from Jubilex. 
*Get Overconfident, and lose a fight.
*Mis-handle cockatrice corpse, turn to stone and die instantly. 
* Get dragged into water by eel or kraken. Solution:  Free action
ring, engage
from distance. 
*By amazing mis-chance, someone gates in Demogorgan.
*Beat to death on element of air.  
*Riders kill me on astral plane. 

I considered carefully these options and devised a strategy to handle
each of them.

In the first couple of levels  I found a magic lamp, which I promptly
blessed and wished for a blessed figurine of an Archon.  He promptly
appeared, armed with Sunsword, and Michael (for such was his name) was
a lethal menace to the legions of Hell, rejoicing at last to have at
the enemies of his God on their own home ground.  Almost immediately
found a SECOND magic lamp.  It went into my bag of holding until I
could figure out what I wanted to do with it.

Down to Asmodeus' level, where a trap door sent me down the next step
to a dismal swamp. Hastily I engraved Elbereth with a bolt of
lightning and had barely cleared my eyes with a unicorn horn when
Jubilex appeared next to me - and turned to flee, as he feared that
name.  I beat him to death as well, then came back up the stairs with
half my available gold.  Asmodeus was right there, and asked me for
cash.  One of my standing rules is "avoid unnecessary combat with
Demon Lords", so I promptly paid him off  and he laughed at me as he
vanished.  Laugh all you like, I'm still standing here and breathing. 
 That's worth more than gold to me.

Of course, his pets stayed behind and I blew my whistle to bring in
Michael and Spike.  Working together, we ripped them apart.

Further down.  Took out the other half of my gold and bought off
Baalzebub.   Found Vorpal Blade, which I used to kill a Jabberwock and
otherwise just carried around as an alternate weapon.

Down to Orcus' level, when I went through a trap door down to the next
level, which turned out to be Rodney's level.  I knew Orcus was above
me, and I wanted his wand of death fully charged.  So I wandered the
level looking for a cockatrice willing to donate its life for the
cause, my previous one in the bag of holding having rotted.    Found
two, but neither left a corpse.  I pondered facing off with Orcus,
then hit on an inspiration - I had recovered some scrolls and wands of
create monster.  I burned through a couple in hopes of generating a
cockatrice, and got a whole slew of monsters including two cockatrices
but neither left a corpse.

Facing up to the inevitable, I plodded up the stairs and immediately
ran into Orcus.  I called in Spike and Michael, then fought Orcus.  He
teleported away, and somehow someone killed Spike.  I engraved
Elbereth, but Orcus kept up his guerrilla harassment.  Eventually
realizing I would never kill him this way, I started walking the long
hard road toward the stairs.  Of course he jumped in and brought his
buddy Yeenoghu too.

Now I was starting to get worried - you know from above that I was
terrified that someone would bring in Demogorgan, and there was a
chance that one of them would do just that.  I reluctantly concluded
there was only one possible choice.  I burned a wish from my wand of
wishing for a blessed cockatrice corpse, and used it to stone both
Orcus and Yeenoghu in two turns.  Then I blew them to bits with force
bolt and recovered Orcus' wand with one charge left.

Explored the level and found Frost Brand, which I picked up and left
Vorpal blade behind in a chest.  I built a cache next to the
downstairs and proceeded down.

I found that clairvoyance from the cornuthaum made it difficult to
know which passages I had explored for treasure and which I had merely
perceived from a distance.  So I took to firing off spells of light so
I would know which branches I had walked down.  Found an Air Elemental
which I tried and failed to tame with my harp.

Continued down through the maze, finding Vlad's tower but continuing
down because I wanted to clear the treasure zoo under Rodney while I
still had fireball, the timer coming close to expiration.   But a trap
door took me past Rodney's entrance down to level 46, where I found
the vibrating square.   I carefully marked it with a gem, a piece of
armor on the left, and a weapon on the right to form an asterisk with
a parenthesis bracketing it, something that NEVER happens in the
dungeon.  Proceed to map back up.   Light ran out, so I began marking
explored area by dropping single gold pieces in the explored area like
bird seed.

One by one, my spell timeouts expired, leaving me nothing but FOD and
Identify.     Found Rodney's entrance on level 44. Explored up and
completed mapping the entire main branch, from level 1 down to level
46.  Proceeded down to Rodney's tower entrance - my intention was not
to engage Rodney, but to clear out the treasure zoo and all the
creatures in the tower outside of Rodney's room itself.   But just as
I reached the level and started on my way with Michael I read a
horrible message on the screen&#8230;

"Buuurrrrrrp!  You have a sad feeling for a moment, then it passes" 


NOOOO!  Michael the Archon, champion of the Celestial Host, had met
his end in a Purple Worm's Intestine!  It cannot be.  I was shocked
for several minutes, then continued on.

Stealth made  the treasure zoo simple, and I used it to attack
creatures one at a time from a distance with my polearm, and when a
group of living creatures conveniently lined up in a row, I zapped 'em
down with FOD.  Recovered a second amulet of life saving in the t-zoo,
then a third on the level above.  There must have been about 30
gremlins here thanks to the water, but I took up position on the far
side of a door and mowed them down by the dozen with FOD.  Then
through the door and used FOD to blast down the Krakens and the Eels.
Now the tower is clear except for Rodney himself, but I'm not prepared
to deal with that yet.

Went back down.  Tried to tame a purple worm as a pet, but it got
killed. Remembered that Michael had been carrying Sunsword and
remembering how useful it would be in Moloch's Sanctum, I tracked down
his killer but, alas, did not find the sword. No time to hunt for it
now - on to Vlad!

Not much to say in here, except that FOD ran out and I found myself 
fighting hand to hand in close quarters in the room, as I didn't
always have room for my halberd.    Killed everything including Vlad
(who was a wuss),  found my fourth amulet of lifesaving and the
Candalabrum of Invocation.   I found it unlikely that anything other
than the Riders instadeath  could stop me now, but I remained
cautious.   However,  my last combat spell timer tripped, and I was
reduced to a combat wombat.   But that was Okay, as the only thing I
still had to do was kill the wizard, go down to the Sanctum, grab the
Amulet and ascend.

But not without some preparation. I went back up to the castle and
began some serious preparation and planning.  I went through all the
caches looking for scrolls of gold detection, potions of confusion,
and booze. I'd heard that reading them while confused would allow one
to detect traps - including magic portals - on a level.  I tested this
theory on level 14, and sure enough felt entrapped  and the portal on
that level stood out like a lighthouse on a stormy night.    I went up
the rest of the way, collecting potions to convert to holy water,
potions of confusion, booze, and scrolls of gold detection.  But when
all was said and done I only had two.

I used the magic lamp to wish for a book of polymorph. I quickly
advanced to skilled in matter spells, getting the failure rate down to
0%.  Polypiling brought out some scrolls of enchant armor , books of
Charm monster (Oh YEAH!), a second fireball book, and a crystal ball
which I put aside as a reserve in case the gold detection scrolls
proved insufficient.   This burdened me, so I left Frost Brand in the
Castle with its mate Fire Brand, since I didn't have the scrolls to
waste on it's upgrading and rustproofing and it was heavy. Besides, I
would be tempted to carry it all the time and would become prey to
malignant auras.  Used the enchant armor to finish armoring up (which
scared me a little, as some of it vibrated unexpectedly) and upgraded
my halberd to +4.

I continue polypiling tools to make a magic marker, but never got one.
 I did, however, tick off a peaceful dwarf when he got in the way of a
polymorph shot and got turned into a bugbear for his pains.  I didn't
want to lose telepathy, so I ran away from him and avoided him every
time I came through that level (level 19) again.   I actually wrote in
my notes "DO NOT KILL THE BUGBEAR ON LEVEL 19", I was so afraid of the
consequences.

Did some more sacrificing in the hopes of more stuff and to reconcile
so I could make Holy Water.  Got a bunch of nothing books.

I thought about burning my last wish for a scroll of charging for my
marker, but I wanted that wish for the planes.  Wandered around and
pondered carefully, Then had a brain storm.

Remember the 0:0 wand in the bones pile on level 12?  

Hurrying down there, Shoshana picked up the wand and promptly blessed
it.  She then burned the last wish in the castle wand for a scroll of
charging and used it on the bones wand. Result: Wand of wishing (1:3).

All RIGHT!  

I burned a wish for another scroll of charging, and used it charge up
my marker.  This allowed me to write scrolls of gold detection and
complete my ascension kit.

Lets see - magic resistance, check. reflection, check. Levitation,
check.  Food (30 or so c-rations), check.  Armor class of -37, check. 
Magicbane, check. Polearm  for killing Death, check.  FOD for killing
Famine and Pestilence, check.  Means of finding the portal - redundant
two, check.  Scroll of charging, check.  One uncursed scroll of 
genocide, check.  One book of charm monster, check.   One ring of
conflict, check.  Holy water (10 potions), check.     All set!

At this point, all my spell timers were out.  I burdened myself with
one (and preferably two) copies of each book I would need for the rest
of the game - two in case one turned out to be too faint to read.  But
before that there was one more chore I had to do.

While I was in Gehennom the first time Shoshana had twice encountered
cats which reminded of her long dead Shadow, who had died above the
Oracle level. She had tamed them with tripe rations and named them
Xena 2 and Meow Mix.  She had led them up the levels out of Gehennom
and up to the castle, where they had promptly fallen back through
trapdoors into the Valley of the Shadow of Death. Being soft-hearted,
she couldn't leave those cats in Hell. So she went back down, re-tamed
them with tripe, then used the magic whistle to take them with her
first to the Castle, then through the Castle and up to the level
above, where (with the moat re-melted) they would find it impossible
to stumble back into the infernal regions.  She released them on level
24, figuring that cats that could survive in the Infernal regions
would have no trouble surviving in a simple dungeon.    She forgot
that they wouldn't be able to cross Medusa's pond.     Anyway, having
performed this small act of mercy she  marched back down to Rodney's
tower.

I was halfway though Hell when I looked that my armor class had gone
from -37 to -27! Wha?  I must have lost my protection!

For a moment I considered collecting all the gold in hell, then
heading back up to minetown and re-buying protection from the priest
there. But I decided no, it would take too long and given my high
level (25) there might not be enough.  Besides, I'd gotten psyched up
for the descent and wasn't ready to abort.  It was also 12 AM real
time, and I wanted to end this.  I would just have to depend on my God
(out-of-game), my FOUR amulets of life saving, and my 350 hit points.

So down to Rodney's tower  until I stood in the room adjoining his
chamber.  I then took out the books and read them all at the same
time, so that I would have them all and they would all go out at the
exact same time, reducing unpredictability.    Then I dumped all the
books in Rodney's tower - I figured it would all be over in 20000
turns one way or the other, anyway. I got rid of everything (including
all the gold) that I didn't absolutely need, remembering a quote from
Return of the King: "We won't need much on that Road, and at it's end
nothing."  So I resolved to travel light, dumping everything except a
small collection of gems which my character Shoshana had become
attached to.  Diamonds are a girl's best friend, even when that girl
is a level 23 Sorceress (uhmmm.. Miracle Worker) who looks more like
Lassie than  like Brittany.

All set. Deep breath, all prayers said .. on with the ring of
levitation. Turn: 80124.

 A blast with a wand of digging through the wall. The look of surprise
on Rodney's face.  He had just enough time to quaff a potion of speed
before a FOD on the next move changed his expression to first a
grimace of pain, then a rictus of death.

Huh.  80000 turns and that's IT? What a wimp.   
The Vampire Lord and other dead friend put up a fight but were quickly
vanished.  I grabbed the book and ran down through the maze to the
vibrating square.   Find a silver saber which I resolve to test on the
Vampires in the sanctum.

Turn 80586. Perform ritual to open Moloch's sanctum.  Fight my way
down. through first a graveyard, where I tamed a purple worm using
charm monster.  His name, of course, was "Burrrrp!"

Fought my way through the priests with Fireball, missile, and FOD. 
This drained all my energy so I avoided combat while re-charging. 
There was a flash of light and I was surrounded by a posse of really
tough monsters, including two cockatrices!  I feared an instadeath
from stoning, so I cast charm monster, and 8 of the ten creatures
(including both cocks) turned friendly. The remaining two are quickly
dispatched.  I explore around the sanctum looking for a door.

I get the message "Double Trouble!"  Huh? But Rodney's not here
&#8230; oh. A quick look with telepathy shows two Wizards of Yendor in
the sanctuary with the High Priest.  Nuts.  Wait &#8230; this could
work to my advantage &#8230; with a grim smile Shoshana slipped on her
ring of conflict and opened the door.

Shoshana had hoped that the two wizards and the priest would get in a
knock-down drag-out and kill each other, then she would take the
weakened victor. It didn't quite work - one of the Rodneys did indeed
start punching and kicking at the priest with all the force of a
whiffle bat, but the other and the priest himself came after her. The
Priest got in a Cause Wounds and Rodney hit with the touch of death
which, fortunately, failed.  After a few turns of unsuccessful
evading, Shoshana said "To hell with this&#8230; wait a minute .. this
IS Hell. Whatever." And blasted the first Rodney and the High Priest
with Finger of Death.  She closed her eyes against the expected
wide-angle disintegration beam as Moloch avenged his servant, but no
such bolt materialized.  The second Rodney reached down and picked up
the Amulet, putting it on with a grin of ecstatic triumph.  This
turned out to be a mistake as, absorbed with the amulet, he had no
defense against the death beam that took him in the chest, returning
his face to his usual death-mask.

There were TWO amulets of Yendor on the corpse. Fortunately, Shoshana
had memorized Identify, and so was quickly able to distinguish between
the cheap plastic imitation and the real thing, which she promptly
took and named. Yee-hah!  Objective complete. Time for egress.  Turn:
81086.

A long and boring ascent through Gehennom follows, broken by an
occasional monster summoning, a "mysterious force" a time or two, and
a single malignant aura absorbed by magic bane.  The ascent was
hastened by the fact that , on the way down, Shoshana had used a pick
axe to cut a direct path through the maze from one staircase to the
other, allowing her to not waste time and simply dash from point to
point. The mysterious force harrassed, but did not, stop, her ascent.

The monotony was broken on Orcus' level when Rodney appeared right by
the stairs.

"So thou thought thou couldst kill me fool."  

"Sigh.  No, Rodney, I KNEW I could kill you. Not only that, I know I
can do it again! FINGER OF DEATH!"

Silly person.  Using Magicbane, Shoshana carved "DORK" into his
forehead so that if he came back again he'd have something to remember
her by.   Continue up, stopping on Juibilex's level to retrieve a
cached book of cancellation and memorize that at failure rate 0.

Turn 82070, arrive at castle. Shoshana did a little dance of joy
because now, outside of Hell, her chances of running into Demogorgan
were infinitesimal - one more small victory in a very long war.  Also,
that means the end of the #$%$#%$ mysterious force that kept knocking
her back downstairs.  Continue up, stop at Fort Ludios to replenish
food from the cached c- and k- rations there.  Turn 82603 : One last
check to make sure I still have the real amulet, then up the stairs
and onto the Plane of Earth.

"So thou thought thou couldst, kill me fool!"  
Shoshana suppressed a grin at the sight of the brilliantly angry,
serious figure with the word "DORK" emblazoned prominently on his
forehead.  "You AGAIN?"  She raised a fist, palm facing her, and
extended the third digit. "Do you know what this means?"

"It means you are childish!" 

"Noooo&#8230;" she said as she turned the finger around to point at
Rodney.  "It means FINGER OF DEATH!"

Ouch.     

An Elven king was right near by and got turned into FODder for his
trouble.  Rodney left a book of Dig which Shoshana memorized. She then
used confused gold detection to find the portal, then rapidly cut her
way there with wands of digging. Before entering the plane of air, she
pulled out a scroll of gold detection, put on her rings of conflict
and levitation, and pulled out a unicorn horn and a wand of
teleportation. Thus prepared, she hit the plane of Air on turn 82691.

Rapidly she confused herself with a time-out spell, then used gold
detection to find the portal.  Once that was located, an application
of unicorn horn cleared up the confusion and she ran for the portal,
maneuvering like an American football fullback through the squadrons
of Air Elementals who tried to tackle her.  She burned out her wand of
teleportation zapping them away, and was finally caught by one. She
cut her way out with Finger of Death, then continued running east.
Twice she was nearly surrounded by Air Elementals, but a quick Charm
Monster turned them on each other while she kept running for the exit,
finally reaching it on turn 82741 with only minimal damage.

"So thou thought thou couldst kill me, fool!"  

Shoshana turned ashen pale. "Y-y-you?  I thought you never came above
the plane of Earth!"

"You were wrong!  Your great mistake was to think me dead, and now you
shall pay."

"No, Rodney, YOUR mistake was that you didn't learn from our last five
encounters. FINGER OF DEATH!"

As he went down for the sixth time, Shoshana muttered to herself "Next
time, you IDIOT, find some means of magic resistance before you tackle
me again.   How many fingers of death does it take?"

The rest of the level was boring.  Find the portal using confused
gold, then duck and weave around the inhabitants to the exit on turn
82785.

Up to water.  Still dodging, she avoided contact with everything but
used her +4 Halberd to engage anyone who needed fighting, as she
didn&#8217;t want an electrical creature to disintegrate her
equipment.  She burned her last two gold detection to find the portal
and stepped through on turn 82831.

At last! The Astral plane! 

You sense excitement, alarm, and hostility in the air!   All the work,
all the battles, all the preparation, have come down to this moment.

"Your desire for conflict will be fulfilled!"  A hostile angel and
some kind of mage materialized right next to Shoshana, but for the
moment she paid them no mind. Instead, she slipped on her blindfold to
take her bearings using telepathy.

Famine on the left, Pestilence on the right, death in the middle.
Hmmm&#8230; I know that if I guess correctly which is my Deity's alter
this battle will be much easier, allowing me to avoid 2 of the 3
horsemen (the angels and priests are mostly filler - my real fear are
the horsemen).

Hmm&#8230; I see that two of the three Sanctii are inhabited by only
the high priest, while the third one is inhabited by a person called
"the student of metals".  Must be a monk or something &#8230; which
sounds neutral to me.  I'll make for that alter.  But first things
first.

I'm being ineffectually wailed on by the angel and the mage. THIS is
the moment I've been saving my wand of wishing for all along&#8230; I
produce the wand and wish for a blessed cockatrice corpse. Which I
receive. Shoshana's face lights up with a fierce and evil grin. Two
bashes later, marvellous statues of an angel and a magician decorate
the halls of the astral plane.

Head off to the door on the left.     Stand off from the door about
two squares and fire off "knock". The lock clicks open.

Famine is first through the door and takes a death beam right in the
chest.  Screaming YALALALALALA Shoshana charges the horde waiting for
her, rapidly stoning the lot and fighting her way to the sanctum,
helped by the fact that the ring of conflict's influence tricks most
of them into fighting each other rather than her.    She pushes west
until she starts getting "really attack the angel of <Deity>?"
messages.  Deciding she doesn't want to fight peaceful creatures, she
pulls off the ring of conflict, stones two more angels, then marches
into the door of the Sanctum. As soon as she comes in, the High Priest
of <her deity> greets her by gulping a potion of speed.

What was that?  A High Priest of <Her Deity>?  Can it be?  Did I
actually guess right?

Step foreward and momentarily there is no doubt. Standing on the alter
is the High Priest.  She #chats with him, and sure enough, it is her
High Priest.  He gives her two bits for a celebratory ale in the Rowdy
Rubber Chicken.

Shoshana is stunned, she can't believe this is really happening.
Outside of the game, I can barely believe that, after fourteen years
of playing, I'm actually about to win.  So shocked I am that I
immediately save and backup the game just in case the power fails at
this exact minute.

But the computer doesn't fail. Shoshana is still standing there.  The
High Priest is still standing on the alter. Then he steps aside,
allowing to proceed forward. As if in a dream, she steps forward and
lays the Amulet of Yendor of the Alter&#8230;

An invisible choir sings!-More-
Congratulations, mortal! -more-
In exchange for your services, I grant you the gift of immortality!
-More-
You ascend to the rank of Demigoddess &#8230; 

***********
"And so, here I am." 

"That's quite a story. There's only one question I have." 
"What's that?" 
"How are you going to pay for the drinks with only two gold pieces?" 
"Oh."  Shoshana blushes furiously, then pulls out a few rubies from
her pouch, hands it to the bartender, Itzhak's brother.  "Will this
do."
"It will indeed.  And welcome to the club."  

&#8230; and in the real world, I look up at my watch.  4:45 AM.  I
guess it's time for bed&#8230;

**********

Before I give the dump, a few acknowledgements are in order &#8230; 

First, my (out-of-game) God (I'm a Christian), for seeing me through
and giving me the ability to win this silly thing.

Second, my wife who's put up patiently with all this.  

Third, the writers of the nethack spoiler files and the inhabitants of
rec.games.roguelike.nethack who gave me the data I needed to get
through the game.

And lastly, the dev team, past and present, who made such a great
game!


*******

Incidentally, I was never once seduced by an incubus.  That was my
choice.  My character has self-respect.  And 3 of the 4 real-time days
this happened on were in a new moon.

